## Configuration

Configuration is validated at startup and fails fast on invalid values.

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `APP_ENV` | `development` | `development`, `staging`, or `production` |
| `SERVICE_NAME` | `{{.project_slug}}` | Service identifier |
| `API_TITLE` | `{{.project_name}} API` | Swagger UI title |
| `HTTP_PORT` | `{{.http_port}}` | HTTP listen port |
| `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | `http://localhost:{{.http_port}}` | Public origin used in links |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `info` | Zap level |
| `APP_GIN_MODE` | `auto` | `auto`, `debug`, `release`, or `test`; `GIN_MODE` is owned by Gin |
| `API_DOCS_ENABLED` | `auto` | Docs on in development, off in production |
| `RATE_LIMIT_RPS` | `20` | Per-IP requests per second; `0` disables |
| `RATE_LIMIT_BURST` | `40` | Token-bucket burst |
| `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | empty | Comma-separated browser origins |
| `CORS_ALLOWED_METHODS` | standard methods | Allowed preflight methods |
| `CORS_ALLOWED_HEADERS` | auth/content headers | Allowed preflight headers |
| `CORS_EXPOSED_HEADERS` | `X-Request-ID` | Response headers exposed to browsers |
| `CORS_ALLOW_CREDENTIALS` | `true` | Send credentials; wildcard origins require `false` |
| `CORS_MAX_AGE` | `12h` | Preflight cache duration |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` | empty | Google OAuth client ID |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` | empty | Google OAuth client secret |
| `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URL` | derived | Google OAuth callback URL |
| `OAUTH_SUCCESS_REDIRECT` | `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | Post-login redirect |
| `TRUSTED_PROXIES` | empty | Proxy IPs or CIDRs trusted for client IPs |
| `PPROF_ADDR` | empty | Optional separate pprof listener |

Never commit `.env`. Generated projects receive a local `.env`; production
values must come from the deployment platform.

## Errors and validation

Errors use `application/problem+json` with RFC 9457 fields plus stable `code`
and `request_id` extensions. Validation failures return `422` with field-level
`errors`. The shared response helpers live in `internal/response`.

## Security

- Request IDs, panic recovery, body limits, security headers, timeouts, and
  rate limiting are enabled in the base.
- pprof runs on a separate, opt-in listener.
- CORS rejects wildcard origins because credentials are supported.
- Secrets stay in environment variables and `.env`; never commit them.
- Auth adds Argon2id password hashes, HS256 access tokens, hashed rotating
  refresh sessions, and TOTP. Refresh cookies are Secure/HttpOnly and
  SameSite=Lax; native clients can request body tokens explicitly.


